feat(lpa-horizon): record the first post hoc outcome and declare checks P3-P6

Adds to the readout the outcome of the first post hoc round (LS6 job
3600785) and, before any of them is run, four further analyses:

  P3  inverse stroke association: selection budget per endpoint with
      atrial fibrillation and systolic pressure added, adjusted models,
      and stroke as a first event (censored at infarction or
      revascularization)
  P4  LDL-C calibration with statin divisors 0.6 and 0.5 and with the
      slope among participants not taking a statin
  P5  linearity into the trial's range: bands of predicted Lp(a), a
      spline with a knot at 150 nmol/L, a quadratic term
  P6  descriptive comparison with the trial's published components

lpa_horizon_posthoc2.R sources the pre-registered script unchanged and
takes the first post hoc script's function definitions without running
it; the SLURM wrapper checks both md5s. Synthetic self-test: LS6 job
3600851, 20 checks. The verdict of record cannot change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 


